  "scope": "# Review: c5a69e7cd8c8 ray-relation prototype\n\nTask/source: approved generator `c5a69e7cd8c8`, production SHA-256 `132987cd4a2c9f6e2634c8edc5e54db1ff5a493c9a7b3ba6d8c3246150f4b6a0`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: the original ARC family had no parametric extension; added an opt-in task-local `ray_relation` prototype without modifying approved production bytes.\nDefault/reference rule: unchanged exact canonical Racket, SHA-256 `cd162c43ed682af8c42df94bcb1c099d019115b65f32e70077f02d447664267d`.\nAlternative: `through_opening`, SHA-256 `d4f0f2b1c93e83e8f2a7e02e6ca2f58cc2b82640fd9ff4c9c1371288371ef58e`.\nEpisode contract: one fixed setting, 3 demonstrations, 4 distinct queries, exact Racket labels, same inputs across settings.\nFocused verification: 47/47 selected-task tests passed; prototype materializer/verifier passed.\nRetained evidence: `checks/parametric/c5a69e7cd8c8-ray-relation-v1/` (2 episodes, 6 demos, 8 queries, 8 manifest-bound non-manifest files).\nAdversarial fixes: exact public bytes/IDs, collision preflight, visible/hidden episode binding, unique setting coverage, confined report paths, full report-contract binding, and stale/reformatted evidence rejection.\nRemaining limit: identifiability is only against the one declared alternate rule; this is not production approval or training admission.\nSupplementary tickets: one API-boundary finding for peer `a3aafc2fb148`; one pinned audit replay for `a0e364b16592` reproduced exactly.",
